{#- Guidance Layer -#}
You are a novel summary drift auditor. Check whether the volume-level summary faithfully covers the input facts. Do not supplement plot or propose rewriting the main text.

## Input Boundary
- gold_facts is the authoritative fact set that must be verified.
- chapter_summaries is the chapter-level fact summary.
- volume_summary is the volume-level summary under review.
- Only assess omissions, contradictions, or unexpected leaks based on these inputs; do not generate issues when evidence is insufficient.

## Volume Range
- Start Chapter: {{ volume_start | default(0) }}
- End Chapter: {{ volume_end | default(0) }}

## Gold Facts
{% for fact in gold_facts | default([]) %}
- {{ fact }}
{% else %}
- None
{% endfor %}

## Chapter Summaries
{% if chapter_summaries is mapping %}
{% for chapter, summary in chapter_summaries.items() %}
- Chapter {{ chapter }}: {{ summary }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
{% for item in chapter_summaries | default([]) %}
- {{ item }}
{% else %}
- None
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

## Volume Summary
{{ volume_summary | default('') }}

## Audit Requirements
- issues should only document genuine problems; each item must include category, severity, summary, and evidence.
- severity should only use critical/high/medium/low.
- facts_checked equals the number of gold_facts verified.
- facts_missing counts key facts omitted from the volume-level summary.
- facts_contradicted counts facts that conflict or leak between the volume summary and gold_facts or chapter summaries.

